<section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">Emergency workflow</div><h1 class="section-title">A simple, traceable response process.</h1><p class="section-sub">The workflow expands only when a request is not satisfied, keeping the first response focused and easy to follow.</p><div class="step-list"><div class="step"><div class="step-num">1</div><div><h3 class="mt-0">Hospital creates a request</h3><p class="mb-0">Authorized staff provide the blood group, units, urgency, district, target donor count and non-sensitive instructions.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="step-num">2</div><div><h3 class="mt-0">Stage 1 local matching</h3><p class="mb-0">The system selects verified, eligible, available and consented donors in the request district who have emergency alerts enabled.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="step-num">3</div><div><h3 class="mt-0">Donors respond</h3><p class="mb-0">A donor can accept or decline from the donor portal or from the secure alert link. Hospitals see anonymous donor IDs until acceptance.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="step-num">4</div><div><h3 class="mt-0">Stage 2 wider outreach</h3><p class="mb-0">If needed, matching expands to nearby districts while respecting donors who selected same-district-only alerts.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="step-num">5</div><div><h3 class="mt-0">Stage 3 hospital referral</h3><p class="mb-0">If the request remains unresolved, approved hospitals receive network referrals and can accept or decline coordination support.</p></div></div><div class="step"><div class="step-num">6</div><div><h3 class="mt-0">Close, fulfil or expire</h3><p class="mb-0">The request is completed when the target is reached, manually closed/cancelled, or automatically expired after its configured lifetime.</p></div></div></div></div></section>
